    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"Let the silence be the final, quiet answer...\" That's a very poetic way to put it. It almost sounds like you're saying there's a certain dignity in just... letting go. To stop the struggle and just accept that the story has reached its natural conclusion. Is there really any point in dragging out the epilogue when the main text is already finished?",
